From 27ae1c961a8ea1364e954d1cf59ddcfa6148dfc7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 06:16:41 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-180: GATE 0 receipt - report eHostVisible in the vk
 memory logger, not just eDeviceLocal

The morning gate needs to know WHICH UMA preference ggml_vk_create_buffer_device was granted (:3665-3670), because DeviceLocal|HostVisible and DeviceLocal-alone land on opposite branches of ggml_vk_buffer_write_2d (:8932 memcpy vs :8942 temp-ctx + submit + waitForFences) - a ~5x difference in what every graph input copy costs. Two dead ends checked on source first: the STAGING marker is behind VK_LOG_DEBUG which is COMPILE-TIME (#ifdef GGML_VULKAN_DEBUG, :215-219), not an env var; and the stock logger prints device-vs-host off eDeviceLocal alone (:2606-2607), so it says 'device' for BOTH preferences and cannot tell them apart. Reuses the existing GGML_VK_MEMORY_LOGGER var (:7773) - no new switch - and is inert unless set. Syntax-checked EXIT=0.

Lane: lane-180
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-debug.cpp; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_486.py)
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-debug.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-debug.cpp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-debug.cpp
index 15abd54681..4a2d53445e 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-debug.cpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan-debug.cpp
@@ -19,7 +19,14 @@ void vk_memory_logger::log_allocation(vk_buffer_ref buf_ref, size_t size) {
     std::lock_guard<std::mutex> guard(log_mutex);
     vk_buffer buf = buf_ref.lock();
     const bool device = bool(buf->memory_property_flags & vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eDeviceLocal);
-    const std::string type = device ? "device" : "host";
+    // lane-180: report HOST-VISIBILITY too, not just device-local. On a UMA device
+    // ggml_vk_create_buffer_device tries DeviceLocal|HostVisible|HostCoherent FIRST and falls back
+    // to DeviceLocal alone (:3665-3670) - and those two land on OPPOSITE branches of
+    // ggml_vk_buffer_write_2d (:8932 memcpy vs :8942 temp-ctx + submit + waitForFences), a ~5x
+    // difference in what every graph INPUT copy costs. The old string printed "device" for both.
+    // Diagnostic only: inside a logger that is off unless GGML_VK_MEMORY_LOGGER is set.
+    const bool hostvis = bool(buf->memory_property_flags & vk::MemoryPropertyFlagBits::eHostVisible);
+    const std::string type = std::string(device ? "device" : "host") + (hostvis ? "+hostvisible" : "");
     allocations[buf->buffer] = size;
     total_device += device ? size : 0;
     total_host += device ? 0 : size;
